## 2026-09-24 License-clean coverage: Wikipedia definitions, offline learn-on-miss, attribution (v6.21.15)
Only CC BY-SA Wikipedia from the clean KS store; no downloads. Checklist: `docs/checklists/checklist_wiki_defs_local_learn_v6.21.15.md`.
- `scripts/ks_wiki_defs.py` (`scan`, `store0`, `titles`, `select`): per-doc zstd fetch store `data/ks/fetch/wikipedia/<seg>/` (7.6 GB, page counts match the index on all 41 segments; segment 00000 decoded from the KS1 store, crc-checked) + `titles.npz` (5,552,940 titles); lead candidates through filter v2 (`ks_retrieve.lead`); 1,278,049 pairs from the top 1.2M articles by length (`data/ks/defs/wiki_defs.jsonl`: "What is X?" / "Who was X?" + 78,049 "What does x mean?"; disambiguated and media titles keep their qualifier; single-letter titles skipped; ASCII-folded because the ray decoder emits ASCII only).
- `ray_qa.py`: streaming `build()` (same API, identical output on the old sources, `.jsonl` pair sources with title refs, peak 1.98 GB RSS for 1,445,366 pairs, 688 MB index); idf from non-Wikipedia rows (chat gates unchanged) + `widf` for Wikipedia rows; per-source top-k in `search`; `wgate` for Wikipedia rows (title span must appear in the question, leftover question words must appear in the answer); `QA.ref`; `guide(full=True)`. Rust `adam-qa` ported (overlap/wgate/top-k); Python-Rust parity 92/92 on the old and new index.
- `ray_learn.py`: local-first learn-on-miss (`AMNI_LEARN_LOCAL=1` default; web only with `AMNI_LEARN_WEB=1`): KS index hits + title linking + local glosses for the person/place check; two-article agreement must include an on-topic article (or 3+ articles); strong single-article match = on-topic article, top candidate, mx >= 0.7 and 0.1 clear of the runner-up. PERSONAL/TEMPORAL guards kept. Learned rows carry `local` and `license`.
- `gguf_runtime.py` (CRLF): Wikipedia QA answers end with "(Source: Wikipedia — <title>)"; local learned answers "(Source: Wikipedia — <title>. I'll remember this.)"; recalls "(I learned this earlier from Wikipedia — <title>.)". `AMNI_RAY_LEARN` now defaults to 1 (offline).
- Measured: dev 45 = 28 answered / 27 correct (unchanged; "What is an atom?" now from Wikipedia). Web 455 (scratch server): 28 correct / 1 wrong / 426 declined (license-clean baseline 17 / 1 / 437; pre-purge best 18 / 3). NQ[200:400] held, offline learn only: 4 answered, 3 correct by hand (2 by string match), 1 wrong, 196 declined.
- Finding: 80 of 121 core topics (Earth, Water, Moon, Democracy, Gravity, Tide, Honey, Paris, London, DNA, ...) are missing from the clean Wikipedia store; ingest counted ~562k docs as "short" (8.8%), which looks like a filter/ingest bug. Raw was deleted, so recovery needs a re-download with the v2 filter.

