## 2026-09-24 KS1 Knowledge Store prototype: Adam's byte model as a lossless entropy coder
Pages (≤4096 B, paragraph breaks) are stored as range-code bitstreams that make Adam regenerate them exactly. Docs: `docs/ks/{sources,pipeline,filter_report,ks1_results}.md`.
- `amni/compute/ks_codec.py`: `paginate`; integer probability tables (floor(logit·64) → integer exp LUT → 16-bit freqs, floor 1); a vectorised 32-bit carry-less range coder over RayField beams (length-sorted waves via `prime`/`_advance`, works on Rust `adam_ray` and Taichi); `write_store`/`KStore` (pages.bin, GF(17) RGBA directory atlas `dir.ptex` with a check digit and crc16, docs/pagemeta parquet with trust fields, frozen coder identity = algorithm + impl-arch + pack sha256); corrupt-index, crc and frozen-coder guards; `memguard`.
- KS2 (2026-09-25): `ks_codec.CODERS` registers `ks1-v16` and `ks2-clean1` (clean base + `data/clean1` lexicon). The coder identity includes `lex`/`lex_id`; `KStore` hosts several codecs and routes pages by coder. Clean re-encode store: `data/ks/store_clean/<src>/<shard>/` (Wikipedia only), per-shard records under `stores.store_clean` in `data/ks/state/`. Clean coder: 2.007 bpb on held-out Wikipedia vs v16 2.245.
- `amni/compute/ks_retrieve.py`: hashed-stem top-64 inverted index segments (mmapped npy), `KSIndex.search/fetch`, answer sentence and candidate extraction via `ray_learn`.
- `amni/compute/rknow.py` (R-KNOW, 2026-09-25): local Wikipedia factoid QA over `data/ks/index_rknow/wiki_v2` (built by `crates/adam-rknow`): BM25 passages + alias-table title links (`al_*`, `adam-rknow alias`) + in-article pool, GBDT passage rerank (`rknow_prr.json`), typed span candidates, logistic ranker + confidence gate, `factq` gate; Wikidata (`wikifact.ask`) fills empty/low-tier answers at low tier; called from `gguf_runtime._ray_stream` after guide/learned, before learn/rchat.
- `scripts/ks_download.py` (Wikipedia 20231101.en parquet; Grokipedia NDJSON streamed to parquet with a license tag), `scripts/ks_ingest.py` (CEO neutral filter first, hygiene, dedupe, held-out, train-queue stub, index, encode, 1% verify, delete raw, report), `scripts/ks_eval.py` (codec/gpu/nq), `tests/test_ks_codec.py` (11 tests).
- Measured (v16, Rust CPU): Wikipedia 2.19–2.24 bpb, Grokipedia 1.77–1.96 bpb, vs per-page zstd -19 3.8–4.0 and whole-set xz -9e 2.45–2.56; 100% exact; ~0.34–0.39 MB/s per process; NQ[0:200] recall@5 0.56. The 1.5 bpb target is not met yet (model gap); the engine requirements for 1 TB are in `ks1_results.md`.

