## 2026-09-09 Crystal exploration: closed-form probe + hybrid e2e (v6.20.260)

`scripts/crystal_probe.py` builds the crystal at its optimum for fixed folds (folds = reduced-rank input directions, pages = bilinear features on UxU of tanh(x.p), contents by ridge least squares) and scores held-out rel vs the fold floor. Result: q/k projections fold (8 rays 8x8 = rel 0.18/0.16 at L0, 0.33/0.30 at L20, 1.6 bpw u8 full-cell), v/o/MLP do not (0.75-0.95). `e2e_kl_distill.py --param hybrid` puts `RayCrystal` (trainable P,T) on q/k and the k12 lattice elsewhere: L00-03 600 steps KL 1.146 vs lattice-only 0.909. The fold caps the re-routing the output objective needs. Checklist `docs/checklists/checklist_e2e_kl_distill_v1.md`.

## 2026-09-08 Operator crystal: fold-dimension floor (v6.20.259)

Measured on the 3B (nib bake, 8k real tokens, held-out 25%): the best k-dimensional fold of x with a linear readout (reduced-rank regression of the true W) has rel floor
L0 q_proj k=16/32/64/128: 0.212/0.175/0.139/0.103 | L20 q_proj: 0.328/0.288/0.250/0.213 (k=512 -> 0.126) | L20 mlp.up_proj: 0.889/0.859/0.821/0.773 (k=1024 -> 0.462).
`OpCrystal` sees x through 2*n_ray dims, so 8 rays = 16 dims. G0 on the 8B q_proj (8 rays, 48x48, 400 steps): rel 0.41 at a 36 bpw full-cell container, still above its linear floor. MLP inputs are full-rank: no ray count under ~1000 dims gets an MLP under rel 0.5, and MLPs are 2/3 of the params. Post-hoc, the crystal is closed on MLPs; designed-in it needs the model trained with per-layer input bottlenecks first. Earlier the same day: end-to-end KL run with the crystal in layers 0-3 (8 rays, 1.52 bpw container) moved KL 7.95 -> 7.91 in 25 steps vs the lattice 6.09 -> 3.05; stopped.

## 2026-09-08 End-to-end KL distill harness (v6.20.258)

`scripts/e2e_kl_distill.py`: student parameterization swapped into layers [start,end) of the frozen 3B bake, trained on KL(teacher||student) over the final logits on the real calib mix, gradient through the frozen remainder (`Swap` toggles module.forward; teacher pass and student pass per step). Score = held-out KL nats + argmax agreement + the same blocks' reconstruction rel. First run L00-03 spectral g64 k12 (0.896 bpw container, 300 steps, 28k tokens): **KL 6.09 -> 1.25, argmax 0.06 -> 0.51, block rel 1.77 -> 1.50**. The student that speaks grammatical English reconstructs the teacher's hidden state WORSE (rel 1.5) than the block-distilled one that produced `??????` (rel 0.2-0.5): the output objective decouples from weight/activation reconstruction. Snap container is int8/coef (8.25 bpw); disk rate = `gf17_spectral_pack.py`. `--gen_only 1` reloads snaps (approximate gains). Checklist `docs/checklists/checklist_e2e_kl_distill_v1.md`.

## 2026-09-08 Sub-1 bpw honest ledger: calibration mirage, flowmap, state LUT (v6.20.257)

- **`scripts/gf17_spectral_distill.py` `calib()` is now a real mix** (wikitext-103 val + `data/distill_corpus_real_v2.jsonl` chats via the granite chat template + repo code, `AMNI_CALIB=synth` restores the old six-sentence loop). Every pre-09-07 block number "under the int4 bar" was memorization of six sentences: k12 L00-01 rel 0.093 synth vs **0.484 real** (bar 0.138). Real-data ladder on the 8B tied teacher (`TS.TIED`): k16 0.443 @1.07 bpw, k24 0.342 @1.33 bpw. Lattice ceiling g=64 k40 = 1.58 bpw. Backup `backups/gf17_spectral_distill.py.v6.20.253.bak`.
- **`scripts/act_spectrum_probe.py`, `scripts/bit_yield_probe.py`** written (activation-covariance water-filling rate; per-bit output yield of the int4 codes). Not yet run to completion.
- **`scripts/flowmap_v1..v5.py`** (`exports/flowmap/`): word-sorted 2D map (PCA strip sort, spectral, PMI) + flow field. Findings: single flow vector per texel = 12.3 bits/tok (unigram 10.8); every sort is a hub star (top-40 tokens in one corner, R50 0.85-0.9, neighbor align 0.99, random sort included); excess over the unigram null is 14-19% of transitions and still points at the hubs; one-word LUT KL to prior 1.4-2.8 bits (= bigram); resolution ladder mip0 8.72 / mip2 7.0 / mip4 4.8 / mip6 2.4 bits; hierarchical modulation mip4 base + 4-bit refinement: coarse 5.6->4.3 bits given word, refinement 4.0->1.7 given coarse+word (mip2 address 6.0 bits vs 12.6 flat). Rule: never score a multimodal cloud by its mean; no sparsity credit in the ledger.
- **`scripts/state_lut_probe.py`, `scripts/state_lut_v2.py`** (`exports/state_lut/`): 3B bits/tok = 4.245 wiki / 5.689 chat. Quantized state -> LUT: layer-20 counts K=4k/32k/262k = 8.95/9.06/9.42 bits; final-norm counts K=4k/32k = 8.54/8.74; distilled (model's own top-32 per cell) K=1k/8k/64k = 7.98/7.87/8.08 bits, argmax agreement with the 3B 0.29/0.34/0.37. The readout is not a K-cell table for K<=64k at 128 PCA dims; bits come from the fine state.
- Checklists: `docs/checklists/checklist_sub1_3b_k12_sweep_v1.md`, `checklist_flowmap_v1.md`.

