- **Keepalive/watchdog hidden WMI spawn (v6.20.216):** `adam_keepalive.ps1`↔`adam_watchdog.ps1` WMI `Win32_Process::Create` respawn (job-breakaway) never passed `-WindowStyle Hidden` in the `CommandLine` string, unlike the Start-Process fallback — every respawn popped a visible console. Added `-WindowStyle Hidden` to all 3 WMI spawn sites (keepalive→watchdog; watchdog→keepalive healthz-down + version-lag paths). Ops fix, no cos impact.
- **Bootstrap missing `_candidate_model_paths` (v6.20.217):** `detect_model()` in `amni/bootstrap.py` called a function that was never defined anywhere in the repo — crashed `amni_serve.py` at import time on EVERY boot (before the port could bind), so Adam could never come up locally. Restored `_candidate_model_paths()` mirroring the existing `_candidate_bake_paths()` pattern (`AMNI_MODEL_PATHS` env + `download_base_model()`'s real default target + local/home fallbacks). Verified live boot to healthy `/healthz` + confirmed `delve_adam.is_up()` (Amni-Delve's Adam-online check) now True. Ops fix, no cos impact.
- **Granite self-identification leak sanitized (v6.20.219):** `GraniteAtexChatService.chat()` (`amni/inference/granite_atex_svc.py`) is the shared generation choke point behind both `/v1/chat/completions` (via `chat_persona`) and the in-process `/delve` room's direct `svc.chat()` call. Under unusual LaTeX+roleplay prompts the base model (`ibm-granite/granite-4.1-3b`) sometimes substitutes its own name for `\Phi` — output now regex-sanitized (`\Granite`/`\granite` -> `\Phi`, backslash-prefixed only, plain-text "Granite" mentions untouched). Live-verified in the Delve room.
- **tier2_template_lut relevance gate wired up (v6.20.220):** `_check_relevance()` in `amni/inference/adam_loop.py` was a designed opt-in cross-encoder filter on tier2's retrieved "template" lessons, but `relevance_svc` was never passed at construction (`amni/adam.py`) — the `if self.relevance_svc is None:return True` default meant it was permanently fail-open, system-wide, letting tier2 blend in cosine-nearby-but-irrelevant past lessons (found via a bomb-refusal lesson bleeding into an unrelated math question). Now wired to `relevance_svc=self.svc` — reuses the already-loaded model as its own judge, no new model/VRAM, one extra short generation call per tier2 candidate. Live-verified: tier2 now correctly declines to fire on the previously-misfiring query, falling through to tier3_cold with an honest answer instead.
- **Delve recap + tier2 relevance/streak (v6.20.218):** Adam repeated near-identical text every round in long delve debates — `hub.py render()`'s `inproc` (Adam) branch always rendered the FULL transcript from turn 0, so `adam_loop.py` tier2 template retrieval (ungated by `_verify_gate`, unlike tier1/1.5) kept re-matching the same stored lesson because static sysmsg/phase_extra boilerplate dominated the embedding every round; the shallow `_check_relevance` judge only checked topic-level relevance, so `_refine_with_template`'s "use the SAME approach and structure" produced near-verbatim paraphrases. Recall itself was explicitly NOT disabled (older lessons legitimately help newer questions) — fixed via 3 targeted changes: (1) `hub.py` `_recap()`/`_note_recap()` (hooked into `add()`) build a structural (VERDICT-line-aware) ≤300-char recap after every non-Adam turn; `render()`'s Adam branch now prompts from that recap + "respond to this specific point" instead of the full history, falling back to full-transcript only when no recap exists yet (`cold_block` long-term memory pack untouched). (2) `adam_loop.py` `_check_relevance` sharpened to demand SPECIFIC-point relevance (not same-topic) and focuses the judge on the last 400 chars of a long query. (3) `adam_loop.py` `_tier2_streak_ok()` circuit-breaks a template key after `AMNI_TIER2_REPEAT_CAP` (default 2) consecutive reuses — skips only that key via `continue`, never blocks tier2 wholesale. 19/19 mocked unit tests pass (`tests/test_delve_recap_v6_20_216.py`, `tests/test_adam_tier2_streak_relevance_v6_20_216.py`); pyright shows zero new issues vs pre-edit backups. Not yet confirmed against a live delve session. Cos=1 (no weight/PTEX changes, orchestration-layer only).
- **Port claim pre-load (v6.20.223):** dual amni_serve boots racing (delve autostart vs healer) each loaded the full bake before the loser died at uvicorn bind — 20GB Modified-Page-List storm, Available=0, system-wide lag (live-caught 2026-07-29 23:02). `scripts/amni_serve.py` `_claim_port()` now binds+listens+HOLDS the socket at top of main() BEFORE any heavy import/model load; healthy occupant (GET /healthz via `_probe_health`) → adopt + exit 0 in ~6s with no load; unresponsive occupant → cleared (old `_free_port_if_occupied`, which previously ran unconditionally and KILLED healthy serves on every boot) + one retry. Held socket handed to uvicorn `Server(Config(...)).run(sockets=[_pguard])` — no rebind race. Pairs with Amni-Delve v3.5.39 atomic `O_CREAT|O_EXCL` launch lock in `delve_adam.start()`. Ops fix, no cos impact.

