## Agentic loop safety rails (v6.20.223, 2026-07-26)
`amni/serve/agentic.py` — the ReAct loop now fails LOUDLY instead of silently, because a silent
failure downstream became a FABRICATION (empty answer -> Delve chat fallback -> invented run output).
- **Tool names self-repair.** `_repair_tool()` = curated alias table FIRST (another framework's names:
  write_file, file_ensure_dir, bash, pytest...), difflib SECOND. Auto-corrects and runs in the same
  step; placeholder junk (`{{}}`, `<tool>`) is never guessed. Repeat offenders force-correct.
- **The loop ALWAYS emits `final`.** max_steps and timeout used to end the generator with no verdict,
  so the endpoint returned `answer:""`. `_synth_final()` builds a truthful summary from
  actually-successful steps only, flags INCOMPLETE, and WARNS about files edited that the goal never
  named. Never claim success. Keep this property in any rewrite.
- **`http_get` is the ONLY network path a skill-using agent has (v6.20.238, 2026-08-15).**
  `run_python` blocks `urllib`/`requests`/`socket` via `_DANGEROUS_PYTHON`; `shell`'s `_SHELL_ALLOW`
  has no `curl`; `web` is DDG-search-and-distill. So "fetch this endpoint and paste the body" was
  impossible until now, and Adam correctly reported local URLs as unreachable. `http_get` is GET-only
  and **loopback-only** (`AMNI_HTTP_GET_HOSTS` extends it) precisely so this stays a "verify a local
  service" tool and not general egress — do not widen it by adding curl to the shell allowlist.
- **`_ABS_RE` must not match inside a URL (v6.20.238).** It matched the `p:/` of `http://` and ran it
  through `_shorten_abs`, so `_tidy` reported `http://127.0.0.1:8795/api/keyring` as `httapi/keyring`
  — a fetch of the right endpoint reported as a different one. The `(?<![A-Za-z0-9])` lookbehind
  keeps drive-letter shortening while leaving URLs intact. Any future path-prettifier needs the same
  guard.
- **`_synth_final` no longer answers a non-question (v6.20.237, 2026-08-15).** Its numeric branch was
  gated on `_numgoal = re.search(r'\d', goal)` — a BARE DIGIT, so any goal containing any number was
  treated as a math question and got `The answer is X (from calc).` as its entire reply. A braid
  ledger handoff (LaTeX + measurements) therefore came back as `The answer is 16.88194302 (from
  calc)` where `16.88194302 = sqrt(285)` and 285 was nowhere in the task. Now `_is_numeric_goal()`
  requires a real compute demand (compute/calculate/evaluate/how many/`what is the value`/an
  operator between digits/`log2(`…) AND `_LEDGER_GOAL_RX` must NOT match (LOCK:/STATUS:/OWNERS:/
  catalog/steelman/board state), AND a tool from `_NUMTOOLS` must actually have run. Keep all three
  conditions — dropping any one restores the fabrication.
- **Exhaustion verifies.** `_exhaust_verify()` prefers the project's real tests (test_run +
  `unittest discover -s <dir> -t <dir>`) over executing an arbitrary artifact — a library file
  "running clean" proves nothing, so that case reports VERIFY PARTIAL, not OK.
- **Write guards.** Contentless `file_write` is blocked (it used to create 0-byte files and destroy
  the deliverable); fence extraction tolerates an unclosed ``` from truncated output; variant
  filenames (foo.2.py when foo.py exists) are refused — the tests import the ORIGINAL name.

## st_frombuffer_patch is thread-safe (2026-07-26)
`amni/inference/st_frombuffer_patch.py` replaces safetensors' loader for the ROCm torch ABI. It kept
ONE file handle and did `seek()` then `read()` per tensor — while `transformers.core_model_loading`
materializes tensors in a **ThreadPoolExecutor**. Concurrent seeks interleaved, so reads returned the
wrong bytes or zero bytes. Symptoms: intermittent boot crash `both buffer length (0) and count (-1)
must not be 0` around 95% of weight loading, and — worse — **silently wrong tensor values**.
Now lock-guarded, with short-read detection (raises naming the key) and zero-length tensor support.
`tests/test_st_frombuffer_threadsafe.py` reproduces the corruption on the pre-fix file. Do not remove
the lock for "speed" — the read is microseconds, the corruption is invisible.

## Delve measured verdict: cube / airplane-LUT / emb (2026-07-30)

Authoritative doc: `docs/airplane_stack_verdict.md`. 21 experiments on `downloaded_models/granite-4.0-350m`; every figure traces to a JSON in `docs/`. **These probes used PQ/INT4/matmul as instruments to price the thesis — they are not architecture recommendations. GF(17) lossless + TMU-first stand.**

Test scripts (all in `tests/`): `cube_sharing_curve.py`, `airplane_lut_ctx.py`, `airplane_lut_diag.py`, `airplane_v2_activation.py`, `airplane_v3_firing_codes.py`, `airplane_v4_state_key.py`, `airplane_v5_mutual_info.py`, `airplane_v6_code_ceiling.py`, `emb_pq_price.py`, `emb_pq_build_artifact.py`, `emb_pq_integration_check.py`, `emb_fidelity_behaviour_curve.py`, `emb_hybrid_hot_cold.py`, `weight_entropy_orthogonality.py`, `weight_entropy_coder.py`, `lut_vs_matmul_fair.py`.

| Line | Measured | Status |
|---|---|---|
| Addressing vs arithmetic | gather **8.81x (B=1) - 46.67x (B=512)** vs fastest matmul | **TMU-first CONFIRMED** |
| Reconstruct-then-multiply | 160-237 us, batch-invariant, ~2.4-3.5x slower than matmul @ B=1 | **never do this** |
| Sub-bit texture trunk | r 2.65->74.32, bpw 6.03->0.2153, rel-F **0.893->0.998**, alpha_all **0.03** | **DEAD** (climb-r executed, failed 6/6) |
| Teacher-match firing LUT | token-argmax ceiling 0.48185; best learned-code Bayes **0.69177** | **DEAD** |
| INT4 context entropy coding | 1.31% per-layer block entropy but only **0.0188%** realizable after model table | **DEAD** |
| Cross-layer weight sharing | mean abs off-diagonal cosine **0.000499** | **DEAD** (matrices orthogonal) |
| ~2 bpw emb silent-swap | `ds4_8bit` built (26,214,560 B, 7.84x, min cos 0.918) but **argmax_agreement 0.586 +/- 0.024** | **NOT SHIPPABLE as drop-in** |
| Hot-fp16 / cold-PQ hybrid | max **0.942** and that costs 84.94 MB emb alone | **FAIL** |
| Config space / 10^27 as payload | block-entropy headroom 0.44% pooled | **capacity, not payload** |

**Two rules this added to the repo's practice:** (1) a reconstruction metric is not a behaviour metric — `ds2_K256` has row cos **0.995** and argmax agreement **0.822**, so any codec must be gated on `argmax_agreement` against a control-validated harness (`control_identity` must return exactly 1.000); (2) the 84.934656 MB figure has **two frames** (2.8T envelope at 0.000243 bpw vs this 350m model at 1.9283 bpw / 8.30x) and mixing them produced a fictional "48.52 MB free" that survived six rounds.

### GF(17) tier fidelity (measured 2026-07-30)
`tests/emb_gf17_tier_behaviour.py` -> `docs/emb_gf17_tier_behaviour.json`. On `embed_tokens`, argmax_agreement vs fp32: **d3_only 0.85993 (FAIL)**, **d3_d2 0.99072 (PASS)**, d3_d2_d1 0.99910, 4-tier **1.00000 / KL 0.0**. So progressive streaming needs **d3+d2 resident (10 bits/weight)**, not d3 alone. GF(17) at 4 digits is 20 bits/weight = 1.25x fp16 -> its value is bit-exactness + streaming, NOT density. Reffelt is bit-exact for id->digits->id; bit-exactness for fp16->digits->fp16 requires a **rank/LUT bijection** (65,536 fp16 patterns into 83,521 ids = 1.27x surplus), not absmax scaling — absmax leaves max_abs_weight_err 4.51e-06. Three codec families (PQ, INT8, GF17) lie on one fidelity-per-bit curve: **the embedding needs ~8 bits/weight for behaviour, whatever the scheme.**

